<entry dateCreated="2005-06-23T16:08:17Z" dateModified="2026-09-28T20:31:37Z" id="mba-_89b79930-93cb-4af5-be86-bea62f1de26a" guid="89b79930-93cb-4af5-be86-bea62f1de26a">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="seh"><text>mba-</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="prefix"/>
<variant>
<form lang="seh"><text>mb-</text></form>
<trait name ="environment" value="/ _ a"/>
<trait name ="environment" value="/ _ i"/>
<trait name ="environment" value="/ _ u"/>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="prefix"/>
</variant>
<sense id="5adef85a-9ff2-477b-a967-a5d519664767">
<grammatical-info value="Verbo">
<trait name="type" value="inflAffix"/>
<trait name="Verbo-slot" value="mba"/></grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>COHES</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="pt"><text>COHES</text></gloss>
<definition>
<form lang="en"><text>thematic continuity, -ing</text></form>
<form lang="pt"><text>continuidade de tema, -ando</text></form>
</definition>
<example>
<form lang="seh"><text>mbauponyera throwing stone, mbumala they ended friendship mbamphata grabing the rabbit,</text></form>
</example>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>^ this is not working - changed _ ~[ to ~_...[, now it works; It has a number of functions: Participle, Discourse connector (like a conjuction), as an Exortative (ex mbatidyeni "let's eat"); It seldom occurs with t/a marker: (and always has Subj w/ it) mb-a-khakhosomola "and he was coughing" mba-mu-dafuna "having wanted" (past participle idiomatically = if you wanted to); mbadzati kudya "having not yet eaten, before he ate" mbadzati dealt with as a unit (see senrt.db) ADV because it is an exception; +PART +Subject ±Tense ±Tense2 ±Object +RootE +VF; (MCC subj requires tense rule not true here); ??cf q above mbakhakhosomola has subj! also mbamudafuna "if you wanted" - yes, mba can take subject; mbakhatimpasa the participle can take 2 tenses (kha- da-) and can take subject and object marker; mbo |no example for this; Question: What is mbo really? I think it is a dialectal form of mba-</text></form>
</note>
<note type="phonology">
<form lang="en"><text>alt: <span lang="seh">mb / _ i / _ u / _ a |eg mb-u-mala mbundikwewa mba-a-panga; mba</span></text></form>
</note>
</sense>
</entry>

